{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556268-banff-canada","id":1556268,"title":"Banff, Canada","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-06T15:41:54-08:00","id":1556268,"title":"Banff, Canada","content":"Without spoiling much, <i>weird shit</i> is growing in Banff's caves, blatantly monstrous tissue that does <i>not</i> trigger Quiescence.<br /> <br /> My first thoughts were crossovery. From a crossover perspective, what could this stuff be?<br /> <br /> For purists, however, from a purely mage perspective what <i>is</i> this stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T16:55:08-08:00","id":1556269,"title":"","content":"It could be the flesh orchard holding one of the Artifacts of the Dethroned Queen (from <i>Reign of the Exarchs</i>).<br /> <br /> It can be a Ecstasy (see <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 38), an Aedes of Life linked to the Primal Wilds, the native tribes of that area tell tales of the lakes being used for healing and in spiritual ceremonies, these powerful symbols resonate with Supernal Truths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T17:10:56-08:00","id":1556270,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly....<br /> <br /> A Verge is where the Fallen World metaphysically brushes up against one of the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> An Aedes is the exact opposite, where the Supernal brushes up against the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Similar, but still distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T17:23:42-08:00","id":1556272,"title":"","content":"Yep, I think that is accurate. One detail of note though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Signs of Sorcery, page 34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Many Aedes are found within Supernal Verges, however, which only serves to muddy the waters further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural phenomena can stack, a Hallow at a graveyard might have an Avernian Gate, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-06-2025, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T19:47:16-08:00","id":1556277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556268-banff-canada?p=1556270#post1556270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly....<br /> <br /> A Verge is where the Fallen World metaphysically brushes up against one of the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> An Aedes is the exact opposite, where the Supernal brushes up against the Fallen World.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Verge is where the Supernal directly intrudes upon Phenomonal reality. An Aedes is wholly within the Supernal and rarely have direct impact on the Fallen World save for subtle things like resonance or the occasional strange lights or weird quirks of probability.<br /> <br /> From a purely Mage perspective, if it doesn't trigger Quiescence then it's not a Supernal or Abyssal phenomenon, including Proximus Blessings, which leaves Mysteries of unspecified other nature.<br /> <br /> From a specifically crossover perspective, weird flesh could be something to do with vampires, Claimed, Created, the God-Machine, or the type of phenomenon that might contribute to or derive from the Divergence, or stranger fare like a displaced experiment from ancient Irem, a gap in the Underworld's storage of the occasional dead body, or the product of some sort of nightmarish pledge between the caves and one of the Fae.<br /> <br /> &quot;Flesh where flesh should not be&quot; is pretty ground-level as far as weird stuff goes \u2014 figuring out what it could be would require more details to narrow the scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T09:12:38-08:00","id":1556299,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> My crossover thought was an Insatiable at least a hundred to a hundred and fifty years old, with extreme power, but who has forgotten <i>how</i> to revert to hunan form, having acquired a Ban involving passive-only feeding.<br /> <br /> From a purely mage perspective i agree with the idea of it being three things at once:<br /> \u25cf A Primal Wilds Aedes.<br /> \u25cf A Primal Wilds Verge.<br /> and,<br /> \u25cf The shallowest reach of an Iris to a Primal Wilds Emanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}